1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,198
The Five-Minute Morning.

3
00:00:03,198 --> 00:00:05,844
My alarm rings, and I turn it off.

4
00:00:05,844 --> 00:00:08,271
I close my eyes for just a second.

5
00:00:08,271 --> 00:00:12,135
When I open them again, Mom is standing in my doorway with my backpack.

6
00:00:12,412 --> 00:00:14,343
Good morning, sleepyhead.

7
00:00:14,343 --> 00:00:16,218
We've got five minutes.

8
00:00:16,218 --> 00:00:18,249
Your breakfast is on the table.

9
00:00:18,532 --> 00:00:19,922
Five minutes?

10
00:00:19,922 --> 00:00:21,536
That can't be right.

11
00:00:21,536 --> 00:00:25,463
I jump out of bed, pull on my clothes, and discover a problem.

12
00:00:25,463 --> 00:00:27,547
Has anyone seen my other shoe?

13
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,001
Which one?

14
00:00:29,001 --> 00:00:31,428
The left one or the one you're standing on?

15
00:00:31,708 --> 00:00:33,056
I look down.

16
00:00:33,056 --> 00:00:35,514
One foot is already wearing a sneaker.

17
00:00:35,514 --> 00:00:36,931
Very funny.

18
00:00:36,931 --> 00:00:38,535
I need the other one.

19
00:00:38,535 --> 00:00:41,431
It's white, and it usually lives next to this one.

20
00:00:41,716 --> 00:00:43,272
Check by the door.

21
00:00:43,272 --> 00:00:45,376
You took them off there yesterday.

22
00:00:45,652 --> 00:00:49,583
I find Dad's boots, Ben's sandals, and one tennis ball.

23
00:00:49,583 --> 00:00:51,208
No white sneaker.

24
00:00:51,208 --> 00:00:53,823
Then I hear a small voice from the living room.

25
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,312
Found it!

26
00:00:55,312 --> 00:00:57,854
My stuffed bear was using it as a boat.

27
00:00:58,132 --> 00:00:59,740
Of course he was.

28
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:02,011
I put it on and race to the kitchen.

29
00:01:02,011 --> 00:01:05,251
Mom hands me a banana and a sandwich wrapped in paper.

30
00:01:05,524 --> 00:01:07,268
Breakfast to go today.

31
00:01:07,268 --> 00:01:10,486
Tomorrow, let's put everything by the door before bed.

32
00:01:10,756 --> 00:01:12,166
I'm ready now.

33
00:01:12,166 --> 00:01:13,312
Wait.

34
00:01:13,312 --> 00:01:14,979
Where's my backpack?

35
00:01:15,244 --> 00:01:17,256
On your back, Captain.

36
00:01:17,476 --> 00:01:19,116
I reach behind me.

37
00:01:19,116 --> 00:01:20,626
He's right again.

38
00:01:20,626 --> 00:01:25,074
We make it outside with matching shoes, breakfast, and one whole minute to spare.

39
00:01:25,074 --> 00:01:28,105
Tonight, I'm checking my bag before I go to sleep.

40
00:01:28,105 --> 00:01:30,563
I'm also hiding my shoes from that bear.
